      "content": {
        "id": "a3f6ead1-1ad3-34b0-a6aa-84b547587b46",
        "contentType": "STORY",
        "title": "SMIC profit more than triples on AI-driven chip demand", // 职位
        "description": "",
        "summary": "China's largest ‌contract chipmaker, Semiconductor Manufacturing ‌International Corp , reported on Thursday second-quarter profit ​more than tripled from a year earlier, beating analyst estimates, as demand for AI-related chips ‌remained robust. Profit ⁠attributable to shareholders came in at $479.2 million, nearly double ⁠the average analyst estimate of $253.4 million compiled by LSEG. Revenue ​rose 36% ​to more ​than $3 billion, topping ‌the $2.8 billion analysts had forecast, LSEG data showed.",
        "pubDate": "2026-08-13T09:37:58Z",
